WEBVTT

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.040
Let me cross, already!

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.370
If I can't get my goods to the
port island, it'll hurt my business!

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.830
No one goes in or out while
the case is under investigation!

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.830
Damn it, I have a job to do!

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.450
Don't make me keep saying it!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.750
You know...

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.040
This is a lot of fuss over the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:37.160
My father had this obsessive
hobby of exploring Midend.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:43.120
I had him take me there several times,
to that desert of death.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:50.200
A great fairy scholar discovered the
<i>Black Fairy Tome</i> in Midend long ago.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.500
It's the result of deciphering 52 epigraphs.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.500
Your dad went missing, didn't he?

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:02.500
On his 17th outing, he went
to Midend and never came back.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.000
What will you do now?

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.290
Once things calm down, I'll go to Westald.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:12.410
Lady Sweet the demon queen is a
wanted woman wherever she goes,

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:15.750
but I guess you <i>would</i> be
safe if you crossed the sea.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.080
Yes, and besides... doesn't it sound like fun?

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.500
Hey!

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.200
At Dorothea HQ, we're going to ask you in
detail about your connection to Veronica Thorn.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.080
Yes, I realize that.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.330
For your own safety, please don't
approach the administrative building!

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.750
Please move back a bit more!

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.290
How did it go?

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.290
Hey, come on!

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:46.450
We looked all over, but found no
one matching Eajey's description.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:50.870
We can't keep people and their goods
from coming and going indefinitely.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:54.540
We'll probably be forced to lift the
blockade come tomorrow morning.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.290
But to go back to Rondacia emptyhanded...

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.580
No...

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.830
Even like this, I still have options.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:09.540
Please stand back!

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.790
For your own safety, please don't
approach the administrative building!

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.750
Stand back! The blockade is scheduled
to be lifted by tomorrow!

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.410
I'll do what I must.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.450
"Episode 17"
"Balance on Sand"

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.250
"Dorothea HQ"

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:35.450
You're telling me the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i>
was stolen by Gui Carlin?!

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.500
Yes, ma'am. The information must have leaked.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:44.580
Also, Gui Carlin weren't the only
ones after the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.950
There were others as well?

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.750
What can you tell me?

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.040
I apologize for calling you in here,
Director Nein Auler.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.660
My name is Damien Carme. I research fairies.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.790
Carme?

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:22.580
As in Michelle Carme, the Fairy Soldier creator?

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.910
I'm her great-great-grandson,
or something like that.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:31.540
I don't know her firsthand, of course.
We might as well be unrelated.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.620
We met him once before in Isharat,

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.450
at the residence of a fairy
scholar named Cain Distarol.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.910
He was together with Ver... with Veronica Thorn.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.080
Very interesting.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.750
I have a request to make.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.700
Would you mind stepping outside?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.250
Huh?

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.410
Why?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:56.660
There's something I very much want to tell you.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:04:01.120
But just you, the director of Dorothea.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:03.540
Very well.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:04.750
Director!

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.250
That's enough, Marlya. It's her call.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.410
Let's go.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:19.870
Well?

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:24.200
But before that, I am not Damien Carme.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.250
What?

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:30.450
It's not "Carme." My real name is... Albastora.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:34.950
My family had its reasons
for dropping that name.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:40.080
You're a descendant of Crucia Albastora,
who wrote the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> ?

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.450
Yes, and that's why I know.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.580
What do you know?

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.870
All the contents of the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.080
Thank you.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.160
Sure.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.830
Are you thinking about Veronica?

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:15.580
Not just about her.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:20.160
The <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> is a classified
document dealing with fairies,

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.750
so Unified Zesskia is trying
to gather and manage it.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:24.790
Right.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:28.790
I understand that, but what
about the other people?

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:34.000
Ver, that Damien guy,
and Gui Carlin, for instance.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.290
I wonder why they want it.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:43.620
The so-called <i>Fairy Tome</i> is
largely divided into five pieces.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:49.370
Hel S. Bellwood's <i>Original Text</i> ,
and Jay B. Mercer's <i>Blue Fairy Tome</i> .

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:56.000
Also, Timothy Connor's <i>Red Fairy Tome</i>
and Colen Thor's <i>White Fairy Tome</i> .

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.950
And then, Crucia Albastora's <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:03.000
Was that right?

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.160
Yeah.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:08.160
Of those, only the
<i>Black Fairy Tome</i> doesn't exist.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.250
Doesn't exist?

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.290
At this point it was about 200 years ago.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:17.870
There was a man who tried to collect the five
fairy tomes, and compile them into one book.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.410
His name was... Alan Bach?

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:24.370
Yeah. However, only the
contents of the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i>

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:28.370
were removed from that finished book.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:31.750
Then, what we're searching for is...

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.750
A reproduction that
Alan Bach hid away, it seems.

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:39.370
A manuscript he deliberately split
into nine pieces and encoded.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.950
He went to the trouble of hiding it...

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:45.870
Were people after the
<i>Black Fairy Tome</i> from the start?

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:51.580
Maybe. Is it worth that much?
And is there some other reason?

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.910
Why tell me?

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:05.950
It's only the gist. You can't misuse that.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:10.830
And all that was written in what
Alan Bach collected was an overview.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:16.750
But reading it would probably make
some people want the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:23.750
That's why we Albastoras deleted those
parts before they got out into the world.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.040
Looks like you failed to
get rid of it completely.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:31.660
Alan Bach secretly retained a
copy of the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:36.950
And now, there are some
who're trying to assemble it.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.910
Gui Carlin.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.120
Not just them.

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.750
There are others, who are more dangerous.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:52.330
We're... Unified Zesskia is basically
gathering together the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i>

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:55.120
for the sake of peace, right?

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.580
It's because, during the War of Unification,

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:02.660
each kingdom endlessly sent Fairy Soldiers
and artificial fairies into battle.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.370
It made the damage even worse.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:12.620
If the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> were to fall into
somebody's hands, bad things might happen.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.290
Something tragic, like that war.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:19.700
Everyone would suffer in sadness,
and go through hard times.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:25.000
We'll perform our duty...
so that doesn't happen.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:28.910
Yeah, that's right.

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.910
I've had my fill of such things.

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:39.580
Fairy Minister Bellwood, may I come in?

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:43.620
I-I apologize, Minister. I was told it's urgent.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.950
Just a moment.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:55.790
It's a bit of a mess in here.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:01.500
You were working first thing in the morning?

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:03.830
I was looking into something.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:05.790
Is this about the port island incident?

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:06.660
Yes, sir.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:10.000
First, regarding the item
seized from the trading vessel.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:14.660
It was the ninth part of the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> .
The so-called <i>Black Nine</i> .

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:15.580
Oh!

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.540
But, unfortunately...

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.200
I see.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:24.830
I left it up to Dorothea to deal
with any unforeseen situations,

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.200
but that was a miscalculation.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.950
There's no excuse I can offer. However...

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:36.120
We've confirmed it was
Gui Carlin that stole <i>Black Nine</i> .

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.870
That figures.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:43.910
We of Dorothea intend to use
this chance to root out Gui Carlin.

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:46.000
I have no objection.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:51.580
They've caused nothing but harm for
Unified Zesskia from the start.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:54.120
When I submit the proposal
to the prime minister,

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:57.620
I would be most thankful for your support.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:02.620
It may not be much, but I'll do whatever I can.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.450
Thank you.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.950
That reminds me, Minister.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.450
Yes, what is it?

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:18.950
More than half of the <i>Black Fairy Tome</i> is
already under Unified Zesskia's control.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.830
Yes. Six parts, including the <i>Black Four</i>

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:26.330
confiscated from Gui Carlin's Ears,
Gilbert Warlock.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.410
Three parts remain.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:33.040
And, naturally, the Ministry of Fairies
is working on decoding it.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:36.540
Does that... interest you?

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:42.080
Some say, within is written
the reason Tupal collapsed,

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:47.750
and its entire realm turned into
the desert of death, Midend.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.000
Even if...

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:54.790
Even if that's true, it's not
something man should know.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:56.700
Perhaps.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:08.040
I'll have some water.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.250
As you wish.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:15.580
Since Warlock was arrested, it's been hard
for Gui Carlin to operate in Rondacia.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:20.500
That makes it a good refuge for you,
with them out to kill you.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:24.160
You're after me too, aren't you?

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.580
Is it because I'm attractive?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.870
It's because you're a criminal.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.450
I'm willing to let the past
be water under the bridge.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:42.540
In that case, you could always
just drink it all instead.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:43.910
Don't joke around.

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:50.370
Tell me what you know about Gui Carlin.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:57.250
Every last thing.
Dorothea won't chase you anymore.

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:58.580
I promise.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.200
Drink.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.830
Then I'll do it.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:11.620
You probably don't trust me,
but neither do I, you.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.410
Earn my trust.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:21.160
Trust me, Sweetie.

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:37.660
You're sure of this?

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:38.750
Yes, sir.

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:42.950
Everyone listed there has
close ties with Gui Carlin,

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:49.410
and can be considered the equivalent
of members... or even executives.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:53.120
But there are a number of
businessmen named here

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:57.830
who've supported us since
during the War of Unification.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:00.910
Even high officials of the unified government...

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:08.290
Once we arrest all these people,
we'd better hope this wasn't a mistake.

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:11.290
I will take full responsibility.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:17.410
You're saying to fire you, if it's an error?

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:20.790
I don't mind if it comes to that.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.200
Very well.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.330
Do it.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:24.290
Yes, sir!

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:28.910
Yes.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.700
So, please make those arrangements.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.290
Yes, boss! Gladly!

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:35.950
"Informant: 'Buz' Sebastian"

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:38.330
Listen up, it's for the boss.
Do this right, you guys!

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:39.450
Yessir!

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:41.950
What'd you do to these guys?

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:44.370
Nothing in particular.

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:47.750
So, boss, we'd love for you to accept this!

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.790
"Evening party venue"
"Escreque"

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.500
Um, what?

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:08.330
Nothing.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:11.540
That really looks great on you, though.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.540
A-As if!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.910
Boss, there he is.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:20.700
People call the guy "The Party King."

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:23.410
He's the art dealer, Hellner Falk.

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:28.410
At a glance, he looks absurdly rich, and nast--

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:31.950
I mean, look at him.

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:34.580
They say he took advantage of
the War of Unification's chaos

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.620
to swipe treasure from multiple nations.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:44.250
He's crooked, but he pays off the right people,
which I guess makes him high society.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.040
All right, stick to the plan.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.580
Yes, boss.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.330
Impressive, boss.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.790
Launch the operation.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.040
Understood.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:13.330
I'll explain the matter to the
Minister of Foreign Affairs.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:17.000
I apologize. But it has to come
from you, Vice-Minister.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.870
Foreign Affairs Vice-Minister Nick Reimer.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:24.540
Come with us.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.790
Director Nein Auler, of Dorothea?

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:29.790
What is this, all of a sudden?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:33.750
You're capable enough to be considered
the next Foreign Affairs Minister.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:37.950
You already know what this is,
don't you? It's about Gui Carlin.

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.870
Wh-What does that have to do with me?

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.450
You don't know?

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.250
"Fuzan"

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:55.750
There's nothing here.

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:57.120
But then, of course not.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:58.450
Yeah.

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:02.540
This is where you and I first met.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:07.120
Didn't we come face to face at
some security briefing before that?

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.540
This is where we really <i>talked</i> .

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:11.160
It was.

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:13.540
We still have some time, right?

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.750
The raid will be just before dawn.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.120
You're not sleepy?

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.330
Then we'll be fine.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.750
I was wondering.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:28.120
Why do you do this work?

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:33.370
Because... this is the only kind
of thing I can manage.

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:34.620
Just fighting.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:37.370
What are you fighting for?

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:42.540
It used to be... At first,
it was to protect my country.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:45.330
If you were a man, you went
into battle as a soldier.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.160
That's how things were.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:49.000
During the War of Unification?

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.000
Yeah.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:55.000
Next thing I knew, I didn't know
how to do anything but fight.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:58.870
Were you fighting after the war ended, too?

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.370
The director took me in.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.700
Until then, well...

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.250
I don't think that's true.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:10.370
Huh?

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:14.200
About knowing nothing but how to fight.

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:18.160
You gave me a helping hand.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:22.580
And thereby dragged you into the fighting.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:27.160
I was called a "cursed child"
from the time I was born.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:30.910
Nothing good happened
when I would get involved.

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:33.000
People died, etc...

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:37.330
I thought everything was my fault.

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:40.410
But that's arrogant.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:43.660
Everyone's living their own lives.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.790
For themselves, for others...

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:52.500
For many different reasons,
they live on, until the end.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:55.870
Everyone's living their own lives.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:18:02.450
They live, and until the end,
that life is theirs.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.950
I was taught a lot of things.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:10.660
It's okay for me to live, too.
My own life, for someone's sake.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:13.000
Facing forward...

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:17.000
...I'm not just fighting, in Dorothea.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:21.370
I talk, I laugh. We eat together.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:26.660
I've found some dear comrades.

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:28.540
Is that right?

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:34.620
It is. That's why I can fight.
Because I have everyone.

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:36.200
Thanks to you.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:40.950
Well then, I'm glad...

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.870
Free.

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:50.750
It will be dawn soon.

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:53.290
Yeah.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:55.830
That it will.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:59.410
"North Eastald Shipping"

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.040
Now!

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:20.830
Go!

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:22.040
Got it!

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:28.540
That hurts! Let me go!

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:30.000
Bran Segaia.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.910
We're with Dorothea. You're under arrest.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:37.410
I can see you don't know how much money
I've invested in Unified Zesskia!

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:41.370
I've known Prime Minister Golbarn
since before unification!

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:43.790
The prime minister approved this, of course.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.370
All right, no struggling.

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:47.700
Ow!

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.330
You're good at that.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:51.200
I learned it from Klara.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:53.040
No wonder.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:54.250
Ow!

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.870
Director Auler.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:04.120
Do you have a report concerning Gui Carlin?

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:08.120
It was stressed to me that
I had better get results.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:12.160
High-handed measures can sometimes
cause strains, after all.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:15.910
If it's to defend the public security
and national prosperity

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:22.040
brought about by peace and order,
sometimes it is unavoidable.

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:23.160
Excuse me.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:31.790
"Dorothea HQ"

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:41.660
Quickly.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:57.450
Where do you plan to take me?

00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:59.120
Eajey...

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:04.450
We found out where he is, but it's shaping
up to be our biggest manhunt in history,

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:07.290
so we're getting away from Rondacia for a while.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:14.120
Meaning, dangerous people might
figure out I'm here, and try to kill me?

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:16.620
Anyway, it's the director's order.

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:19.120
We'll move you somewhere safe.

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:23.410
Damien Albastora. Don't use Ver anymore.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:30.450
On what do you base that?
I haven't forced her to do anything.

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:34.620
But you urge her to work with you, don't you?

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:38.000
She has her reasons.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:41.080
Even if she got her revenge, it'd mean nothing.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:45.830
That's not for me or you to decide.
It's up to her.

00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:48.370
I want to stop Ver!

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.830
Everyone is alone.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:57.750
She might not come back to me again.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.160
I imagine she'll carry it out on her own.

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:04.700
Ver isn't alone.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:08.370
She still has me!

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:41.580
Fairies don't rightfully belong to anyone!

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:43.080
A cultivated Fairy Soldier?!

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:44.870
For my comrades who believe in me!

00:23:44.870 --> 00:23:46.700
Free!

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:48.500
"Next time"
"Dancing Mouse and Broken Horn"

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:48.500
I'm taking you down right here!
